// A list literal made only of a spread of a fresh list `const`, delivered where a wider record
// list is declared (D16443): the `const`'s literal is built at the destination's element, as a
// spread into a push builds it, at every position, in both faces.
//
// Format: scripts/capability-probes/README.md, "Template format".
// @@PRELUDE@@
const s = [{ x: 1 }, { x: 3 }]
// @@VALUE@@
[...s]
// @@TYPE@@
{ x: f64 }[]
// @@PROOF@@
print(v[1].x * 2 + v.length)
// @@WANT@@
8
// @@SKIP@@
is_in_if: the value is a list, not a union — there is no arm to test it against
is_in_while: same
is_in_and: same
is_in_not: same
else_if: same
early_return_guard: same
